knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3424
What it fixes: Nitro builds: dependencies of the RSC environment are bundled, so a package's `react-server` export condition is honoured.
Amended (rc.2, R1): the original hunk's blanket `resolve: { noExternal: true }` also swept
Next's default server-external list (sqlite3's `bindings` helper, typescript) into the compiled
executable, regressing the `turbopack-reports` and `twoslash` deploy-test fixtures — bindings
walks up from its own file to find package.json and no longer finds one inside the binary;
typescript's bare `import.meta` aborts the compile. Carrying `external: [...userSsrExternal]`
alongside `noExternal: true` keeps those packages external under Nitro too, matching the
non-Nitro RSC branch below (`external: userSsrExternal === true ? true : [...] `) and the
pre-#3424 "patches OFF" build output.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3424.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

